      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# SDXL · LITE · Generate\n\nChoose a standard SDXL checkpoint in the single loader. MODEL, both CLIP encoders and VAE come from that checkpoint. Default: installed SDXL Base 1.0. Juggernaut XL and standard SDXL fine-tunes can use this starting recipe. Lightning, Turbo, LCM and Refiner checkpoints need their own recipes; this template is for standard base models.\n\n30 steps / CFG 6 / DPM++ 2M / Karras. Positive and negative prompts are both active. Start near 1024px and tune CFG/steps for the selected checkpoint.\n\nSet prompt and negative prompt, choose size and batch in Resolution, then Queue. Latent uses 4 channels /8.\n\nCanvas Layout JSON is not connected: SDXL requires regional conditioning nodes for area prompting. These templates use normal text conditioning.\n\n### Checked recipe\nSDXL: 30 steps, CFG 6, dpmpp_2m / karras. Sampler profile checks model and latent compatibility. Profiles do not select weights: Base, Turbo, Distilled and Edit checkpoints are not interchangeable. Use a fixed seed when comparing changes; increase size only after the prompt and composition work."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# SDXL · LITE · Generate\n\nChoose a standard SDXL checkpoint in the single loader. MODEL, both CLIP encoders and VAE come from that checkpoint. Default: installed SDXL Base 1.0. Juggernaut XL and standard SDXL fine-tunes can use this starting recipe. Lightning, Turbo, LCM and Refiner checkpoints need their own recipes; this template is for standard base models.\n\n30 steps / CFG 6 / DPM++ 2M / Karras. Positive and negative prompts are both active. Start near 1024px and tune CFG/steps for the selected checkpoint.\n\nSet prompt and negative prompt, choose size and batch in Resolution, then Queue. Latent uses 4 channels /8.\n\nCanvas Layout JSON is not connected: SDXL requires regional conditioning nodes for area prompting. These templates use normal text conditioning.\n\n### Checked recipe\nSDXL: 30 steps, CFG 6, dpmpp_2m / karras. Sampler profile checks model and latent compatibility. Profiles do not select weights: Base, Turbo, Distilled and Edit checkpoints are not interchangeable. Use a fixed seed when comparing changes; increase size only after the prompt and composition work."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
